10
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
Brotherhood (stylised as BrOTHERHOOD) is a 2016 British crime drama
film written, produced and directed by Noel Clarke.

11
00:57:12,000 --> 00:57:18,000
It is the sequel to 2006's Kidulthood and 2008's Adulthood, and
the third and final instalment of The Hood Trilogy.

12
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:30,000
It stars Clarke, Jason Maza (who also co-produced the film), Arnold Oceng, Stormzy,
Cornell John, David Ajala, Shanika Warren-Markland and Adjoa Andoh.

13
01:07:36,000 --> 01:07:42,000
Brotherhood follows Sam (Clarke), now a family man of two
children, being driven back to his criminal lifestyle.

14
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
Clarke initially did not want to make a third film, but eventually returned in 2015
to write, direct and star in the third film of his Hood Trilogy.

15
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
Filming began in London in November.

16
01:23:12,000 --> 01:23:18,000
Brotherhood was screened in the Special Presentations section at the 2016 Toronto
International Film Festival and was released on 29 August 2016.

17
01:28:24,000 --> 01:28:30,000
The film received mixed-to-positive reviews and becoming
the highest-grossing film in the trilogy.

18
01:33:36,000 --> 01:33:42,000
The film explores themes of london, england, ghetto, hood, gang.

19
01:38:48,000 --> 01:38:54,000
The tone is emotional.
